<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_SeveredTentacleFlesh.xml                      FEVERWOOD_TENTACLE_BESTIARY_1

  "A severed tentacle is the only renewable source of the animal's body" —
  design sheet §2b/§6j: the canon dianoga food line (pie from the meat, tea
  from spleen chemicals, cream) needs dianoga BODY, and this is the only way
  to get it without killing the elder being (which cannot be killed, only
  driven off — §2b's own permanent-kill row is per-map, not per-animal).
  Dropped by RM_CompTentacleLimb.Sever()/RM_CompTentacleEye's two upper
  rungs whenever a limb takes severe damage before it can withdraw.

  A plain raw organic resource, same shape as RM_DrainedFluids
  (CreatureBehaviors) — no recipe consumes it yet. The actual pie/tea/cream
  product chain is Cuisine mod territory (FEVERWOOD_DIANOGA_PRISON_1's own
  note: "the owner's 2026-09-14 ruling on that entry already assigned this
  material to the Star Wars Cuisine mod"), out of this item's scope. It IS
  perishable (CompRottable) — real tentacle flesh, not a mineral — same
  posture as vanilla raw meat.

  PLACEHOLDER ART: vanilla meat has no static texPath to crib — it is
  generated per-race by RimWorld/ThingDefGenerator_Meat.cs, which branches on
  body size/flesh type onto one of four fixed atlas paths. RimSage-read this
  pass (Lines 7-127): a non-humanlike, non-insectoid race at baseBodySize
  >= 0.7 gets "Things/Item/Resource/MeatFoodRaw/Meat_Big" — the fitting
  bracket for a limb off something vast — deep-purple tinted, the canon-
  confirmed dianoga colour ("deep purple skin, purple-staining tea",
  FEVERWOOD_DIANOGA_PRISON_1) carried to the free-tier Sekkulaath too, since
  colour is not IP. Same borrowed-texture-plus-tint posture as
  RM_DrainedFluids/RM_ScaldWalkerChitin.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RM_SeveredTentacleFlesh</defName>
    <label>severed tentacle flesh</label>
    <description>A length of thick, rubbery flesh, still faintly warm, cut from a limb of whatever vast thing lives beneath the Fever Wood's pools. It grows back — eventually, on the animal, not in the pack. Traders who know the biome pay well for it; it renders into a rich meat and a strange, purple-tinged tea.</description>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/MeatFoodRaw/Meat_Big</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <color>(90, 30, 110)</color>
      <drawSize>0.9</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>14</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.4</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.7</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>2</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <stackLimit>50</stackLimit>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Rottable">
        <daysToRotStart>5</daysToRotStart>
        <rotDestroys>true</rotDestroys>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
